# What the api image must not contain, and one line here is a security boundary
# rather than a size optimisation: the Dockerfile ends `COPY . .`, and that image
# is published to a registry (ADR-0039), so anything that survives this file is
# shipped — including to whoever pulls it. `.env` and `.env.*` are excluded for
# exactly that reason, not because a build needs them: the app reads its
# configuration from the environment and its signing key from a mounted file.
#
# The rest is build context. `.venv` is 291 MB measured, uploaded on every build
# and copied into the image at /app/.venv — where it does nothing at all, since
# the install below is `--system` (UV_SYSTEM_PYTHON=1) precisely so a dev
# bind-mount over /app cannot shadow it. The caches are regenerated.

.venv
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

.env
.env.*
